{"id": 10450, "name": "Harry Gardner Park", "read": "2026-10-15", "pages": [{"url": "https://www.co.cowlitz.wa.us/1277/Harry-Gardner-Park", "lines": ["-3030) is a 65 acre park along the South Toutle River. It was destroyed by the Mt. St. Helens Eruption and has been recently brought back to life with similar amenities to pre-eruption. | Camping area offers 11 RV sites($25/night) and 11 tent campsites($20/night). | RV sites are equipped with electricity and water connections. | Each site includes a picnic table and fire pit. | There are 2 ADA accessible RV sites and", " sites are equipped with electricity and water connections. | Each site includes a picnic table and fire pit. | There are 2 ADA accessible RV sites and 2 tent sites. | Sewer dump station on site for your use. There is a $5 fee for RV’s not staying at the park. | The park also offers hiking trails, playground equipment and easy access to the South Toutle River for fishing and swimming. | There is a 7 day stay limit. |"]}, {"url": "https://www.co.cowlitz.wa.us/289/Online-Services", "lines": [], "via": "Online Services"}]}
